IMPORT prelude

-- Proceeds of Crime Act 2002, Part 7, section 340 (Interpretation) -- LAYER 1.
-- Target: main (checked on build 1.6.109).
-- Section 340 is "for the purposes of this Part" (s 340(1)); the other modules take the facts its definitions need as inputs and the
-- seat layer asks for the same facts, so the definitions here are reached by the questions about "criminal property", "money laundering",
-- "deposit-taking body" and the rest.
--
-- SHAPE.  A definition that says "means" or "is ... if" answers JUST TRUE when its conditions hold and JUST FALSE when they do not
-- (the text says no in its own words, or, for an "if" that is not "only if", on lawyer-reading (a) of NOTES.md).
-- A definition that says "includes" answers JUST TRUE for the listed thing and NOTHING for anything else.
-- A definition that sends the reader to another instrument (the Electronic Money Regulations 2011, the Financial Services and Markets
-- Act 2000, the Value Added Tax Act 1994, ...) takes the outcome of that instrument as an input and answers NOTHING when it is not met.

§ `Section 340: interpretation`

§§ `s 340(1) and (2): application and criminal conduct`

-- s 340(1) "This section applies for the purposes of this Part" is a lead-in: it fixes where the definitions below are used, and
-- creates no rule (coverage table: inert, reason 1).

-- src:775 | (2) Criminal conduct is conduct which—
-- src:776 | (a) constitutes an offence in any part of the United Kingdom, or
-- src:777 | (b) would constitute an offence in any part of the United Kingdom if it occurred there.
@ref s 340(2) (src:775-777)
GIVEN `the conduct constitutes an offence in any part of the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the conduct would constitute an offence in any part of the United Kingdom if it occurred there` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 340(2) the conduct is criminal conduct` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the conduct constitutes an offence in any part of the United Kingdom` OR `the conduct would constitute an offence in any part of the United Kingdom if it occurred there`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Criminal conduct is conduct which"

§§ `s 340(3) to (8): criminal property, benefit`

-- src:778 | (3) Property is criminal property if—
-- src:779 | (a) it constitutes a person’s benefit from criminal conduct or it represents such a benefit (in whole or part and whether directly or indirectly), and
-- src:780 | (b) the alleged offender knows or suspects that it constitutes or represents such a benefit.
@ref s 340(3) (src:778-780)
GIVEN `it constitutes a person's benefit from criminal conduct or it represents such a benefit (in whole or part and whether directly or indirectly)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the alleged offender knows or suspects that it constitutes or represents such a benefit` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 340(3) the property is criminal property` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `it constitutes a person's benefit from criminal conduct or it represents such a benefit (in whole or part and whether directly or indirectly)` AND `the alleged offender knows or suspects that it constitutes or represents such a benefit`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Property is criminal property if" (a failed "if" read as the text's no: marginal reading (a))

-- s 340(4): the three matters are immaterial.  "It is immaterial" says that the matter makes no difference; the rule says so for these three
-- matters and is silent about any other.
-- src:781 | (4) It is immaterial—
-- src:782 | (a) who carried out the conduct;
-- src:783 | (b) who benefited from it;
-- src:784 | (c) whether the conduct occurred before or after the passing of this Act.
@ref s 340(4) (src:781-784)
DECLARE `Matter that is said to be immaterial` IS ONE OF
    `who carried out the conduct`
    `who benefited from the conduct`
    `whether the conduct occurred before or after the passing of the Act`
    `another matter`

GIVEN matter IS A `Matter that is said to be immaterial`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 340(4) the matter is immaterial` MEANS
    CONSIDER matter
    WHEN `who carried out the conduct` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `who benefited from the conduct` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `whether the conduct occurred before or after the passing of the Act` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `another matter` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "It is immaterial" is said of these three matters and of no other

-- src:785 | (5) A person benefits from conduct if he obtains property as a result of or in connection with the conduct.
@ref s 340(5) (src:785)
GIVEN `he obtains property as a result of or in connection with the conduct` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 340(5) the person benefits from the conduct` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `he obtains property as a result of or in connection with the conduct` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person benefits from conduct if he obtains property" (a failed "if" read as the text's no: marginal reading (a))

-- s 340(6): the sum taken to be obtained.  The answer is a number, so "the text gives no sum" is NOTHING.
-- src:786 | (6) If a person obtains a pecuniary advantage as a result of or in connection with conduct, he is to be taken to obtain as a result of or in connection with the conduct a sum of money equal to the value of the pecuniary advantage.
@ref s 340(6) (src:786)
GIVEN `he obtains a pecuniary advantage as a result of or in connection with the conduct` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the value of the pecuniary advantage, in pounds` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 340(6) the sum of money he is taken to obtain, in pounds` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `he obtains a pecuniary advantage as a result of or in connection with the conduct` THEN JUST `the value of the pecuniary advantage, in pounds`
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the rule speaks only of a person who "obtains a pecuniary advantage"

-- src:787 | (7) References to property or a pecuniary advantage obtained in connection with conduct include references to property or a pecuniary advantage obtained in both that connection and some other.
@ref s 340(7) (src:787)
GIVEN `the property or pecuniary advantage was obtained in the connection with the conduct` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was obtained in both that connection and some other` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 340(7) the property or advantage was obtained in connection with the conduct` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the property or pecuniary advantage was obtained in the connection with the conduct` OR `it was obtained in both that connection and some other` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "include references to property or a pecuniary advantage obtained in both that connection and some other"

-- src:788 | (8) If a person benefits from conduct his benefit is the property obtained as a result of or in connection with the conduct.
@ref s 340(8) (src:788)
GIVEN `the property was obtained as a result of or in connection with the conduct by a person who benefits from it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 340(8) the property is his benefit` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the property was obtained as a result of or in connection with the conduct by a person who benefits from it` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "his benefit is the property obtained" ("is" read as a closed definition: fork register)

§§ `s 340(9) and (10): property and interests`

-- src:789 | (9) Property is all property wherever situated and includes—
-- src:790 | (a) money;
-- src:791 | (b) all forms of property, real or personal, heritable or moveable;
-- src:792 | (c) things in action and other intangible or incorporeal property.
@ref s 340(9) (src:789-792)
DECLARE `Kind of thing` IS ONE OF
    money
    `real or personal property`
    `heritable or moveable property`
    `a thing in action or other intangible or incorporeal property`
    `something else`

GIVEN thing IS A `Kind of thing`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 340(9) the thing is property` MEANS
    CONSIDER thing
    WHEN money THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `real or personal property` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `heritable or moveable property` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a thing in action or other intangible or incorporeal property` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `something else` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "Property is all property wherever situated and includes"

-- src:793 | (10) The following rules apply in relation to property—
-- src:794 | (a) property is obtained by a person if he obtains an interest in it;
@ref s 340(10)(a) (src:793-794)
GIVEN `he obtains an interest in it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 340(10)(a) the property is obtained by the person` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `he obtains an interest in it` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "property is obtained by a person if he obtains an interest in it" (a failed "if" read as the text's no: marginal reading (a))

-- src:795 | (b) references to an interest, in relation to land in England and Wales or Northern Ireland, are to any legal estate or equitable interest or power;
@ref s 340(10)(b) (src:795)
GIVEN `it is a legal estate in land in England and Wales or Northern Ireland` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is an equitable interest in land in England and Wales or Northern Ireland` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a power over land in England and Wales or Northern Ireland` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 340(10)(b) the thing is an interest in land in England and Wales or Northern Ireland` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `it is a legal estate in land in England and Wales or Northern Ireland` OR `it is an equitable interest in land in England and Wales or Northern Ireland` OR `it is a power over land in England and Wales or Northern Ireland` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "references to an interest, in relation to land in England and Wales or Northern Ireland, are to any legal estate or equitable interest or power"

-- src:796 | (c) references to an interest, in relation to land in Scotland, are to any estate, interest, servitude or other heritable right in or over land, including a heritable security;
@ref s 340(10)(c) (src:796)
GIVEN `it is an estate, interest, servitude or other heritable right in or over land in Scotland` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a heritable security over land in Scotland` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 340(10)(c) the thing is an interest in land in Scotland` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `it is an estate, interest, servitude or other heritable right in or over land in Scotland` OR `it is a heritable security over land in Scotland` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "references to an interest, in relation to land in Scotland, are to any estate, interest, servitude or other heritable right in or over land, including a heritable security"

-- src:797 | (d) references to an interest, in relation to property other than land, include references to a right (including a right to possession).
@ref s 340(10)(d) (src:797)
GIVEN `it is a right in property other than land` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a right to possession of property other than land` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 340(10)(d) the thing is an interest in property other than land` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `it is a right in property other than land` OR `it is a right to possession of property other than land` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "references to an interest, in relation to property other than land, include references to a right"

§§ `s 340(11): money laundering`

-- src:798 | (11) Money laundering is an act which—
-- src:799 | (a) constitutes an offence under section 327, 328 or 329,
-- src:800 | (b) constitutes an attempt, conspiracy or incitement to commit an offence specified in paragraph (a),
-- src:801 | (c) constitutes aiding, abetting, counselling or procuring the commission of an offence specified in paragraph (a), or
-- src:802 | (d) would constitute an offence specified in paragraph (a), (b) or (c) if done in the United Kingdom.
@ref s 340(11) (src:798-802)
GIVEN `it constitutes an offence under section 327, 328 or 329` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it constitutes an attempt, conspiracy or incitement to commit an offence under section 327, 328 or 329` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it constitutes aiding, abetting, counselling or procuring the commission of an offence under section 327, 328 or 329` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it would constitute an offence in paragraph (a), (b) or (c) if done in the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 340(11) the act is money laundering` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF       `it constitutes an offence under section 327, 328 or 329`
              OR `it constitutes an attempt, conspiracy or incitement to commit an offence under section 327, 328 or 329`
              OR `it constitutes aiding, abetting, counselling or procuring the commission of an offence under section 327, 328 or 329`
              OR `it would constitute an offence in paragraph (a), (b) or (c) if done in the United Kingdom`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Money laundering is an act which"

§§ `s 340(12) to (13): employer, constable`

-- src:803 | (12) For the purposes of a disclosure to a nominated officer—
-- src:804 | (a) references to a person’s employer include any body, association or organisation (including a voluntary organisation) in connection with whose activities the person exercises a function (whether or not for gain or reward), and
-- src:805 | (b) references to employment must be construed accordingly.
@ref s 340(12) (src:803-805)
GIVEN `the body is the person's employer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person exercises a function in connection with the body's activities (whether or not for gain or reward)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 340(12) the body is the person's employer for a disclosure to a nominated officer` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the body is the person's employer` OR `the person exercises a function in connection with the body's activities (whether or not for gain or reward)` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "references to a person's employer include any body, association or organisation"

@ref s 340(12)(b) (src:804-805)
GIVEN `the person is employed by the body` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person exercises a function in connection with the body's activities (whether or not for gain or reward)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 340(12)(b) the person is in employment for a disclosure to a nominated officer` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person is employed by the body` OR `the person exercises a function in connection with the body's activities (whether or not for gain or reward)` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "references to employment must be construed accordingly" (as (a) widens "employer", "employment" widens with it, and the text states no outer limit)

-- src:806 | (13) References to a constable include references to a person authorised for the purposes of this Part by the Director General of the National Crime Agency.
@ref s 340(13) (src:806)
GIVEN `the person is a constable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is authorised for the purposes of this Part by the Director General of the National Crime Agency` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 340(13) the person is a constable for the purposes of this Part` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person is a constable` OR `the person is authorised for the purposes of this Part by the Director General of the National Crime Agency` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "References to a constable include references to a person authorised"

§§ `s 340(14) to (17): bodies and relationships`

-- src:807 | (14) “Deposit-taking body” means—
-- src:808 | (a) a business which engages in the activity of accepting deposits, ...
-- src:809 | (b) the National Savings Bank , or
-- src:810 | (c) a person specified, or of a description specified, in regulations made by the Treasury or the Secretary of State.
-- src:811 | (14A) In subsection (14)(a)—
-- src:812 | (a) the reference to the activity of accepting deposits is a reference to that activity so far as it is, for the time being, a regulated activity for the purposes of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 by virtue of an order under section 22 of that Act, but
-- src:813 | (b) the reference to a business which engages in that activity does not include a person specified, or of a description specified, in regulations made by the Treasury or the Secretary of State.
@ref s 340(14) (src:807-813)
GIVEN `it engages in the activity of accepting deposits, so far as that is a regulated activity for the purposes of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 by virtue of an order under section 22 of that Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a person specified, or of a description specified, in regulations under subsection (14A)(b) as not engaging in that activity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is the National Savings Bank` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a person specified, or of a description specified, in regulations made by the Treasury or the Secretary of State under subsection (14)(c)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 340(14) the person is a deposit-taking body` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF       (    `it engages in the activity of accepting deposits, so far as that is a regulated activity for the purposes of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 by virtue of an order under section 22 of that Act`
                  AND (NOT `it is a person specified, or of a description specified, in regulations under subsection (14A)(b) as not engaging in that activity`))
              OR `it is the National Savings Bank`
              OR `it is a person specified, or of a description specified, in regulations made by the Treasury or the Secretary of State under subsection (14)(c)`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“Deposit-taking body” means"

-- s 340(14B): the duty of the Treasury or the Secretary of State to consult before making regulations is the procedure for making a rule;
-- it is machinery (coverage table: inert, reason 2).

-- src:815 | (14C) “Electronic money institution” has the same meaning as in the Electronic Money Regulations 2011 (S.I. 2011/99) (see regulation 2 of those Regulations).
@ref s 340(14C) (src:815)
GIVEN `it has the same meaning as electronic money institution in regulation 2 of the Electronic Money Regulations 2011` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 340(14C) the person is an electronic money institution` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `it has the same meaning as electronic money institution in regulation 2 of the Electronic Money Regulations 2011` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the meaning is that of regulation 2 of the Electronic Money Regulations 2011 (S.I. 2011/99), which is not among the sources

-- src:816 | (15) “Information order” means an order made under section 339ZH.
@ref s 340(15) (src:816)
GIVEN `it is an order made under section 339ZH` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 340(15) the order is an information order` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `it is an order made under section 339ZH` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“Information order” means an order made under section 339ZH"

-- src:817 | (16) “Payment institution” means an authorised payment institution or a small payment institution (each as defined in regulation 2 of the Payment Services Regulations 2017 (S.I. 2017/752)).
@ref s 340(16) (src:817)
GIVEN `it is an authorised payment institution (as defined in regulation 2 of the Payment Services Regulations 2017)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a small payment institution (as defined in regulation 2 of the Payment Services Regulations 2017)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 340(16) the person is a payment institution` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `it is an authorised payment institution (as defined in regulation 2 of the Payment Services Regulations 2017)` OR `it is a small payment institution (as defined in regulation 2 of the Payment Services Regulations 2017)` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“Payment institution” means an authorised payment institution or a small payment institution"

-- src:818 | (17) “Business relationship” means a business, professional or commercial relationship between a person carrying on business in the regulated sector and a customer or client, where the relationship—
-- src:819 | (a) arises out of the business of that person, and
-- src:820 | (b) is expected by that person, at the time when contact is established, to have an element of duration.
@ref s 340(17) (src:818-820)
GIVEN `it is a business, professional or commercial relationship between a person carrying on business in the regulated sector and a customer or client` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it arises out of the business of that person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that person expects, at the time when contact is established, that it will have an element of duration` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 340(17) the relationship is a business relationship` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF       `it is a business, professional or commercial relationship between a person carrying on business in the regulated sector and a customer or client`
             AND `it arises out of the business of that person`
             AND `that person expects, at the time when contact is established, that it will have an element of duration`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“Business relationship” means"
